## Intuition
Each digit maps to a set of characters, and we need to generate all possible combinations by choosing one character for each digit. This forms a recursive tree where at each level we pick one character corresponding to the current digit and move to the next digit.

A common approach uses string concatenation `current + ch`, but since strings in Java are immutable, this creates a new string object at every recursive call, leading to unnecessary overhead.

## Approach
We use backtracking to build combinations. Instead of string concatenation, we use a `StringBuilder` to efficiently construct the current combination.

At each recursion level:

- Get the characters mapped to the current digit
- Append one character to the current string
- Recurse to the next index
- Backtrack by removing the last character

This avoids repeated string creation and improves performance. We also use a `String[]` for mapping digits to characters for O(1) access.

## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {
    private String[] map = {"", "", "abc", "def", "ghi", "jkl", "mno", "pqrs", "tuv", "wxyz"};

    public List<String> letterCombinations(String digits) {
        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();
        solve(0, new StringBuilder(), digits, result);
        return result;
    }

    private void solve(int i, StringBuilder curr, String digits, List<String> result){
        if(i == digits.length()){
            result.add(curr.toString());
            return;
        }
        String letters = map[digits.charAt(i) - '0'];
        for(char c : letters.toCharArray()){
            curr.append(c);
            solve(i + 1, curr, digits, result);
            curr.deleteCharAt(curr.length() - 1);
        }
    }
}
```

## Complexity
**Time Complexity:** 
O(4^n * n), where n is the length of the input. Each digit can map to up to 4 characters, and each valid combination requires O(n) time to construct.

**Space Complexity:**
O(n) auxiliary space for recursion and StringBuilder (excluding output).
Output space is O(4^n * n) for storing all combinations.
